*Heading
Two rigid bodies on springs joined by a HINGE connector, checked against exact statics
** The construct of a CAE hinge model: each part is tied to a reference point by *MPC BEAM
** (abq2ccx: a *RIGID BODY with a ROT NODE), and a CONN3D2 HINGE joins the two reference
** points.  Body A (reference point 1 at the origin, members 11-13) rests on nine SPRING1
** elements; body B (reference point 3 at d = (0.2, 0.5, -0.1), members 21-23) hangs on the
** hinge and one spring.  The hinge axis is the local 1-direction of orientation AXES,
** e1 = (1, 2, 0.5)/|.|, an oblique axis; the joint offset d is not along it, so the JOIN
** part (node 3 keeps its offset in node 1's turning system) carries rotation terms.
** Forces on members 12 and 22 and a moment on reference point 3 (DOFs 4-6, which
** abq2ccx moves to the ROT NODE).
** Small displacements: 12 unknowns (u, theta of both reference points), 5 hinge
** constraints u_3 - u_1 - theta_1 x d = 0, (theta_3 - theta_1) parallel to e1;
** validate_with_ccx.py solves the system exactly (Lagrange multipliers) and compares
** every printed displacement.
